{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>If HaShem desires us.</b> Indeed its goodness is exceedingly great — on the condition that HaShem desires us, as it says: ״אֶרֶץ אֲשֶׁר ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ דֹּרֵשׁ אֹתָהּ״ (Deuteronomy 11:12), ״וְהָיָה אִם שָׁמֹעַ תִּשְׁמְעוּ וגוֹ׳״ (Deuteronomy 11:13)." "<b>And He will bring us into this land.</b> The opposite of what our colleagues testified in saying ״לֹא נוּכַל לַעֲלוֹת אֶל הָעָם״ (Numbers 13:31) — for indeed the inhabitants of the land will not rise against us at all, as it says: ״יִדְּמוּ כָּאָבֶן עַד יַעֲבֹר עַמְּךָ ה׳״ (Exodus 15:16). And so it was: they made no defense and no preparation to prevent the people from ascending against them." "<b>And He will give it to us.</b> For we saw that no spirit rose in any man against us, and that their intent was to flee." "<b>A land flowing with milk and honey.</b> It is so of itself, without the labor of those who work the soil — as in forests, in the manner of ״וְכָל הָאָרֶץ בָּאוּ בַיַּעַר וַיְהִי דְבַשׁ עַל פְּנֵי הַשָּׂדֶה״ (1 Samuel 14:25). And this would not have been possible if there were any defect in the land or in its air."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:50.025050231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}